    { "id": "268f6ad6-1069-4ce0-a3bc-f744504c2082", "name": "Sticky Note bc0e1868", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote", "typeVersion": 1, "position": [190, 230], "parameters": { "content": "## Config-driven setup\nAll per-run settings (company/brand name, pricing rates, size-tier and discount rules, Airtable base/table, internal notify email, follow-up delay, PDF engine choice) live in the Config node. It runs in parallel off both triggers (includeOtherFields: true) rather than inline in the main chain, because — unlike Demo 1 — the webhook body here carries real per-enquiry data that must not be overwritten.", "color": 6, "width": 320, "height": 260 } },
    { "id": "039b6c37-dcd1-4fdc-8aa8-02ca048cdf4c", "name": "Sticky Note 4c4ac51e", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote", "typeVersion": 1, "position": [990, 150], "parameters": { "content": "## Idempotency guard\nRequires the caller to supply a stable enquiryId. \"Check Existing Quote\" uses alwaysOutputData: true so a no-match still produces one item to route on (zero-item-safety pattern); \"Determine Duplicate Status\" then checks whether that item has a real id — present only on an actual match.", "color": 4, "width": 480, "height": 200 } },
    { "id": "d6500bc4-c803-4966-9959-fb35ac4098e1", "name": "Sticky Note 907c8a1a", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote", "typeVersion": 1, "position": [1950, 310], "parameters": { "content": "## AI output is untrusted until parsed\nReuses Demo 1's pattern: fence-stripping, JSON.parse in a try/catch, and a schema check before use — plus one extra guard here, since pricing depends on it: every line item's category must be in the allowed enum, or the run fails with a specific message naming the bad value.", "color": 3, "width": 480, "height": 200 } },
    { "id": "7ee41912-4032-4ce5-abd9-45307b419bdf", "name": "Sticky Note ee866240", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote", "typeVersion": 1, "position": [3470, 70], "parameters": { "content": "## E-signature is stubbed, not live\nThis node is disabled by design — no paid e-sign account is wired up. It marks exactly where a real \"create envelope\" API call (DocuSign / Dropbox Sign) would go. The architecture is complete: QTD - Signature Callback Receiver is a real, working webhook ready to mark the Airtable record signed the moment a provider is connected.", "color": 5, "width": 340, "height": 220 } },
    { "id": "580a6b1e-b408-4c8e-a0c8-a59def24ec7a", "name": "Sticky Note 3e4f3eb0", "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote", "typeVersion": 1, "position": [4430, 70], "parameters": { "content": "## Follow-up is a real Wait, not a schedule\nfollowUpDelayMinutes is compressed to 2 minutes for demos; a real deployment would set this to something like 4320 (3 days). n8n's Wait node suspends the execution properly and resumes later regardless of length — it is not subject to the workflow execution timeout while suspended.", "color": 4, "width": 620, "height": 200 } }
